The game got off to a slow start, I was reluctant to ride before I got a 
level
or two for fear of killing myself falling off the horse. I spent a lot of 
time
trying to manage pets without a leash or magic whistle. Theory was I could 
get
some dogs and cats, find a poly trap in the mines and come out riding a 
dragon
or something fancy like that. Didn't work, the only poly trap I found in the
mines, I stepped on, and the next was on DL24, just above the castle. Wes 
didn't
acquire any intrinsics until 16,500 turns into the game, that was poison
resistance. Needless to say I didn't have high expectations up to that 
point.
Telepathy didn't come until 34,250!

Another thing that slowed me down was the absence of ID scrolls, I was well 
into
the game, perhaps even post quest, before I found and price IDed a ?oID.

I normally play wishless, poly-thingless and genoless but I'm always willing 
to
deviate if I think it will make the game more interesting for me. In this 
case,
I got a wish in the mid game from a smoky potion (booze). I had a vision of 
a
dragon riding, magic missile casting knight for this character and I just 
didn't
think I could get there with this low intelligence, so I wished for a +2 
[HoB.
Later when I got the castle wand I wished for ?oCharging, +oMagic Missle 
(that
got me a +oRC), a +oMagic Missile and a +oID (It was a patience thing at 
this
point).

It was a strange game for items found or not found. I found 5 magic markers,
about 4.5 more than normal in my experience. There were 3 magic lamps. On 
the
other hand I never found a [oMR, [T Shirt, =oSD, =oConflict, /oPoly or 
/oCancel.
This latter worried me a lot. I've read here several times about the perils 
of a
c(BoH and without a /oCancel, it seems that could be disastrous. I carried a
sack and kept my b(BoH in the sack when I remembered, but that was a real 
pain.
I didn't get a magic whistle or a key until Orcus level at turn 53,300.

There were plenty of altars and stores. Altars in the main dungeon  were on 
2,
4, 11, 17 and 22 along with two general stores, two large liquor stores and 
a
bookstore. I bought both Holy water and Unholy water in these stores. There 
was
a portal to Ludious on DL11. I had to pray for food once but I had to pray
because of low HP three occasions.

The mine entrance was on DL3 and the first mine level was lit so I cleared 
it
but retreated to the main dungeon when the second mine level was dark. The
entrance to Sokoban was on DL10 and I finished it ASAP, getting the desired 
"oR.
By this time Wes was about XL 7 or 8 so I risked dipping for Excalibur
successfully. On the way back to the mines at the lawful altar on DL4, I
sacrificed a rat just because it was convenient and got Grayswandir for my
trouble. I used Excalibur most of the time because of the searching but 
switched
to Grayswandir when fighting the named demons and when it came time for the 
run
home.

I found a (BoH on the second level of the mines. Minetown was on DL6 with a
cross aligned altar, the bottom was at ML11. I set off the only poly trap I 
was
aware of, spending some time as a hill giant but only losing some dwarven
mithril and a +1 elven cloak. Got my luckstone and headed back. I got 3 
points
of protection from the priest in minetown (the only priests in this game 
were
minetown and the VotD).

About here I felt I had to make a decision about my ranged weapon. I like 
spears
better for a knight but daggers were more plentiful, lighter and give a +2 
to
hit. I decided on the daggers and used them on monsters like (m)mf to soften
them up before engaging them hand to hand. I found 3 +3 daggers (price 
IDed), a
+2 and a couple of +1 early on and these served as my ranged weapons for 
most of
the game. Later when I had a stack of 16 fireproof, +6 elven daggers, I 
found I
really didn't need them.

I stopped at the altar on DL4 to get a few 4 leaf clovers. Not long after I 
gave
a unicorn a couple of IDed gems to max out my luck. (I had a blessed 
touchstone
even though I still didn't have a ?oID).

The next stop was Ludious. I stood a knights move from the door in the first
room and killed the monsters and soldiers one on one, I had to retreat at 
least
once to heal. Then I moved to the second room and did the same thing with 
the
soldiers that couldn't find their way to the first room. Next the dragons 
went
down. I did have to do some jumping to get away and go heal a time or two. I 
got
some white scales and wore them for weight reduction even though I wasn't 
ready
to enchant them yet. Now I went and got a pile of rocks to kill the monsters 
in
the moat.

Finally I froze the moat in front of the back door and unlocked it so the
monsters could come out to fight me. I couldn't control this battlefield as 
well
and had to run once to heal. On the way back I met Croesus. I remembered 
having
close calls with him before. He's one of the most dangerous characters in 
the
dungeon for me, considering my character's development when I normally meet 
him.
After he took me from 90 to 40 HP in one attack, I jumped away and retreated
until I could get him lined up with my /oDeath, so there! I gathered up all 
the
gold and trudged all the way back to minetown to give it to the priest. That 
got
me to 10 points of intrinsic protection.

Still with no MR, I was concerned about getting too deep but didn't know
anything to do but dive. I was relieved to encounter two incubi on DL22 and
managed to get XL 14 with a little hanky panky. So on to the quest back on 
DL16.

I did use a price IDed ?oEA to make some WDSM to get my AC to -20. That 
should
be enough until I am ready to wake the wiz. The quest was uneventful and the
Mirror provided the sought after magic resistance. The water levels were 
made
less tedious by a pair of [WWB.

My backup plan if the wiz should steal the Mirror was a !oHalu and 
Grayswandir.
Luckily it never came to that but I always had them with me once the wiz was 
in
play. Later when I found some silver scales I enchanted them so I could wear 
an
"oLS in place of the "oR. First time in years I'd wore an "oLS.

Medusa was on DL23. I got me another pile of rocks to kill the sea monsters 
from
safe range and then put on my WWB to stroll over and kill her. Actually, I 
think
my "oR killed her, I didn't really see it. I got some c[BoL from the statue 
of
Peresus but never used them since I had a couple of =oLev by this time.

On DL24 I found a poly trap! Visions of my dragon danced in my head. I must 
have
spent a half hour of real time waiting by the poly trap with my pet leashed 
to
me. When I finally got a leocrotta, I gave up. The leocrotta turned out to 
be a
pretty good mount, it's fast (and I zapped it with a /oSM as well) and a 
good
fighter with all those attacks but it's max level wasn't high enough to get 
it
to attack shopkeepers or priests. It always leaves a corpse as best I could 
tell
so my /oUT rescued it a few times. I finally killed it for good coming out 
of
the dungeon with the amulet when I rode into the swamp on my second trip 
through
Juiblex's level.

When I got to the castle on DL25 I was greeted by a master lich. Since I 
already
had the stairs I just beat it to death and got an anthame for my trouble. I 
got
another later in the game, the first time I ever got two in one game. Next 
order
of business was to clear the sea monsters with the ever handy pile of rocks.
I am paranoid when it comes to that drawbridge. I think the only way to do 
it is
the blow it down from a distance and then bridge the moat with a boulder or 
a
/oCold. Well, I had left all my /oStriking somewhere safe and really didn't 
want
to go looking so I put on my [WWB and went around back. I had a =oLev for 
the
traps. There was nothing of real interest in the armory and the dragons 
didn't
give me any better scales. In fact, I only saw one gray dragon and two 
silver in
the dungeon. In the battle that followed with the soldiers, one of them had 
a
/oStriking so I didn't have to go searching.

The castle wand was 0:1 and I already mentioned that I used my wishes on
?oCharging and spell books, though I put it off until I had cleared all of
Gehennom except the last of the wiz's tower and the sanctum. My knight never 
did
become that MM casting terror I was hoping for. My plan now was to clear the
VotD, stash most of my stuff in the castle and press down through Gehennom 
until
I couldn't carry all the stuff I had collected.

Asmodeus was immediately below the VotD. I hit him until he retreated, stood 
on
the downstairs, lured him down when he returned and then beat him to death 
while
I stood on the upstairs. Juiblex was on DL32. I used the old /oDig trick on 
him.
The only character I ever lost beyond the castle was to Juiblex, it was late 
and
I forgot to heal myself. Well, not this time.

Baalzebub was on DL34 and he was dispatched much like Asmodeus. Vlad's 
entrance
was on DL35 and once again he provided no challenge. Orcus was on DL40 and 
he
went down to the staircase tactic. I finally found a magic whistle on Orcus
level. I got careless and got slimed for the first time. Well, time to test 
the
lore that says fire is the cure, it was of course.

I worked my way down to DL46 before I decided I just had too much stuff and 
I
was in danger of reaching the bottom level without knowing it. I tamed a dog 
or
cat or something and stood by a poly trap blowing my magic whistle until I 
got
something bad enough to kill the @'s in the dungeon, turned out to be a mmf.

We level teleported all the way to ML3 and then went to minetown to pillage 
the
place. I left Izchak, albeit alone, and lugged all that stuff back to the
castle, clearing stashes and shops along the way. I lost my mmf to a level
teleporter before I came to the last shop, so I just bought all his 
inventory
and let him live and continued to the castle.

Next I level teleported to the bottom (asked for 60 but got sent to DL48). 
It's
important to me to know when I'm on the bottom because I walk the level
differently. On the other levels I avoid the corners when possible since 
that's
where most of the traps are. On the bottom I have to step on those corner 
square
to avoid having to redo the level if I don't find the VS on the first pass. 
I
had explored most of the level when I found the VS and marked it with the 
Bell
and Candelabrum.

I worked my way back up to the portal to the wiz's tower on DL46, cleared 
the
tower up to but not including waking the wizard. Now I level teleported back 
to
the castle to finish my buffing and polishing. When I was done, Excalibur 
was
+6, Grayswandir +7, my second weapon was a +7 rustproof longsword. I had 
AC -37,
everything blessed and about 30 or 40 b!oFH. I quaffed enough of the b!oFH 
to
get to about 250 HP. That seemed to be enough to be safe but low enough to 
keep
it interesting. Everything that needed to be IDed was, and charging scrolls 
were
written and put in reserve for the 3 /oDeath if necessary. I finally got my 
2 tins
of homemade tengu out hoping to free one ring finger for the trip out. I was
rewarded by feeling "in control" on the first one. I got an ample supply of
?oTele and all 6 of the !oGL I had collected during the game, duly cursed.

I took all the gold and stashed it near the priest of Moloch. and launched 
from
the VotD to DL46 at 62,800. Back through the tower, woke the wizard and 
killed
him with my /oDeath, grabbed the book and levelported to the bottom. Went to 
the
VS and did the deal, descended and held the stairs until I could kill the 
purple
L's that came to greet me. This is where I got the second anthame, already
enchanted to +3.

I worked my way through the graveyard and into the inner sanctum. I was a 
little
nervous because of a disenchanter, a green slime, a mmf and the large number 
of
priests who could cast spells that hurt me bad compared to what the rest of 
the
monsters could do. At some point I killed a cockatrice and used the corpse 
to
make the whole courtyard scene go quickly. It didn't occur to me anything 
was
out of place when Yeenoghu showed up for his statue to be made.

I had already used my ?oLight and /oSDD on the east side of the sanctum when 
my
curiosity got the better of me. All those statues with items in them just 
kept
calling me. Even with the wizard out and about, I just had to go see. When I
broke Yeenoghu's statue I found The Amulet of Yendor! Thinking this to be a
fake, I tried to put it in my bag and it wouldn't go. I even used my ID 
spell
and it drained my power as I IDed it. I guess Yeenoghu must have killed the
priest and stolen the amulet before he came to attack me!

At this point I didn't even bother with the inner sanctum, I just headed for 
the
castle. I used my c!oGL on the no teleport levels and ?oTele on most of the
others to hasten my ascent. Alas, that mysterious force was working 
overtime.

It took forever and the wiz came around a few times to make me nervous. I 
used
my last c!oGL to exit Juiblex level but ultimately got pulled back there two
more times. I lost my leocrotta, Croesus, (named when I tamed a dog in Ft.
Ludious) when I carelessly rode him into the water. I used my /oCold and 
pick
axe hoping to find his corpse but only the saddle remained!

Somewhere along the way I took the time to tame a couple of domestic animals 
and
then stood by a poly trap blowing my magic whistle until I got me another 
dragon
to ride. I stopped off in the VotD and gave the stashed money to the priest 
for
3 more points of protection. Then I let my dragon loose on him for his
spell books. back in the castle I wrote up a few more scrolls I expected to 
use
in the planes, c?oGD and taming to name a couple.

On the way out I had to deal with a disenchanter. I dropped the amulet so I
could magic missile it to death and when I went back to get the amulet, it 
was
gone! After reflection, I decided only my dragon could have it. My /oProbing
confirmed my suspicion. Hmmm... wonder if there is a trick here? If I rode
upstairs in Gehennom with my mount carrying the amulet, would the mount be
subject to the mysterious force?

My dragon ultimately got killed by a bad bounce when I shot a death ray at 
the
wizard. I forget why I didn't use my /oUT but I ended up riding a pony to 
the
Planes. I didn't take the trouble to get unburdened for the elemental 
planes.

Earth is never any trouble, well, except for starting with the wizard! Once 
that
was done I used a crystal ball to locate the portal. Seems like it's always 
in
the same place. I burned 2 /oDig getting there. I dumped all my /oDig and my
pick ax before hopping through the portal.

Air can be a little scary sometimes but I carried a couple of b!oFH outside 
my
bag and I did use one of them when my HP went below 100 while being pummeled 
by
debris. I used a c?oGD (or was it a ?oGD while confused) and got 3 $. I went
toward the wrong one first but it wasn't terribly out of the way when I had 
to
go on to the second. I used a ?oTaming while confused to tame two more 
dragons
but I was having trouble keeping them alive so I went on, determined to tame
another on the Astral Plane.

Fire was a piece of cake, used the crystal ball again to locate the portal 
and
made for it, still levitating, fighting as little as practical. On water I
donned my oilskin cloak. Now my only danger was to have my =oLev zapped by 
an
electric eel while over water. I used the crystal ball again to give me an
initial target. The plan was to get into the general vicinity and then use a
/oSDD to home in. That didn't work. I'm starting to think it never did. I 
used
two more c?oGD before I made the connection with the portal.

On arriving on Astral I removed my =oLev, burned an Elbereth into the floor,
dropped my bag and by then the two arch liches had arrived. Of course they 
had
nowhere to retreat and they couldn't attack so I beat them to death at my
leisure. Then a couple of dragons came around so I tamed them. I made a 
stash in
my outer sack, just in case and made sure I was not burdened at this point. 
I
entered on the right side so I went that way first.

I was met by Death, didn't have a problem as he went down to my +7 
Grayswandir
and +7 longsword. I hadn't gotten very far when I met death again. This was 
a
different story, my max HP were down to 173 from 259 before I could kill 
him! I
went back to my stash and dug out 9 b!oFH to take my HP back up to 245. I 
killed
some monsters, teleported a few, jumped whenever possible and when I entered 
the
temple, monsters started retreating! Home sweet home!

After disposing of a priest or two and an angel and an adventurer, I rode my
white dragon over to the altar and put on my 2 =oAdornment. This party in 
the
demigod bar is going to last a long time. A girl with Charisma 20 should 
have a
better time. I whistled for my green dragon and my guardian angel and 
offered
the amulet. I guess my green dragon was eating, but I rode Snow White to
immortality!

